## 11. Features — How Each One Works

### 11.1 🔐 Authentication
1. User fills Login/Register form in `AuthContainer.jsx`
2. `App.jsx` calls `AuthContext.login()` or `register()`
3. `apiFetch("/api/auth/login", {POST})` sends credentials
4. Backend `AuthService` validates → BCrypt password check → JWT generated
5. Token stored in `localStorage`, `currentUser` updated
6. App re-renders → main chat interface shown

### 11.2 💬 Real-Time Messaging
1. User types in ChatWindow input bar → click Send
2. `ChatContext.sendMessage()` → `cryptoEngine.encryptPayload(content)` → returns `{ciphertext, iv}`
3. STOMP `publish({destination: '/app/chat', body: JSON.stringify(messageDto)})`
4. Backend saves to DB → broadcasts to both users via STOMP topics
5. Both ChatContexts receive via subscription → `decryptPayload(content, iv)` → update state → re-render

### 11.3 ✅ Message Status (Ticks)
- **Single grey tick** = Saved to server
- **Double grey tick** = Delivered to receiver's STOMP topic
- **Double blue tick** = Receiver called `POST /api/messages/read/{sender}` → broadcast → sender UI updates

### 11.4 ⌨️ Typing Indicator
1. User types → debounced event fires → `PUBLISH /app/chat/typing {isTyping: true}`
2. Backend broadcasts to `/topic/typing/{receiver}`
3. Receiver's ChatContext shows "typing..." under contact name in sidebar
4. Auto-clears after 3 seconds of no typing activity

### 11.5 📞 Voice & Video Calls (WebRTC)
```
Caller:
1. User clicks audio/video call button
2. navigator.getUserMedia() → gets mic/camera stream
3. Creates RTCPeerConnection
4. Creates SDP offer
5. STOMP PUBLISH /app/call/signal {type: "call-request", callerUsername, callType}

Receiver:
6. IncomingCallOverlay appears → ringtone plays
7. User taps "Accept"
8. Gets local stream → creates RTCPeerConnection
9. Creates SDP answer → PUBLISH back

Both:
10. ICE candidates exchanged via /app/call/signal {type: "candidate", candidate: {...}}
11. WebRTC P2P connection established (direct audio/video stream)

End Call:
12. PUBLISH {type: "call-end"} → both close streams
13. POST /api/calls → saves CallRecord → broadcasts call history update
14. Chat shows system message: "📞 Audio Call • 2:25"
```

### 11.6 👥 Group Chats
1. User opens GroupModal → types group name → selects contacts
2. `POST /api/groups` → ChatGroup saved in DB with Set<User> members
3. Group messages sent with `groupId` field in MessageDto
4. Backend broadcasts to ALL group members' individual topic channels

### 11.7 📱 Status/Stories
1. User creates status in StatusPanel → type: text/image/video, caption, background color
2. `POST /api/statuses` → Status saved with `expiresAt = now + 24 hours`
3. `GET /api/statuses` → returns only non-expired statuses of contacts (+ self)
4. Frontend shows contact ring (green = unseen) → click → full screen story viewer

### 11.8 🌟 Starred Messages
1. Long press/right-click message → "Star" option
2. `POST /api/messages/star/{id}` → toggles `isStarred`
3. StarredModal shows all starred messages filtered from local message state

### 11.9 📌 Pinned Messages
1. Long press message → "Pin" → `POST /api/messages/pin/{id}` → toggles `isPinned`
2. Pinned messages shown at top of chat with pin indicator

### 11.10 😀 Emoji Reactions
1. User taps message → emoji picker appears
2. `POST /api/messages/react/{id}` with `{reaction: "👍"}`
3. DB stores: `"alice:👍,bob:❤️"` (comma-separated key:value)
4. Both users notified via WebSocket with updated full reaction string
5. Frontend parses & displays emoji reactions below bubble

### 11.11 🗓️ Scheduled Messages
1. User opens ScheduledModal → enters message text + picks future date/time
2. `POST /api/scheduled` → ScheduledMessage saved with `sendAt` timestamp
3. Spring `@Scheduled` task (MessagePurgeScheduler) runs every minute
4. When `sendAt <= now` → auto-sends message via MessageService

### 11.12 💨 Vanish Mode
1. User enables vanish mode via VanishModeModal for a specific conversation
2. ConversationVanishMode record created for that chat pair
3. After message is read (`readAt` set) → ConversationVanishModeService deletes it
4. Periodic scheduler `MessagePurgeScheduler` cleans up expired vanish messages

### 11.13 🔒 Chat Lock
1. User opens ChatLockModal → sets a PIN code
2. PIN stored only in browser localStorage (NOT sent to backend — privacy first)
3. On next open of that chat → PIN prompt appears
4. Correct PIN → chat unlocks

### 11.14 💣 Self-Destruct Messages
1. User sets `selfDestructSeconds` when composing (e.g., 30 seconds)
2. Message sent with `expiresAt = timestamp + seconds`
3. `MessagePurgeScheduler` (@Scheduled every minute) queries expired messages
4. Deletes from DB → broadcasts deletion event to both users
5. Both clients remove the message from UI

### 11.15 📊 Analytics Dashboard
AnalyticsPanel.jsx shows:
- Total messages sent/received
- Total calls made + duration
- AI feature usage count
- Most active contacts

### 11.16 🔒 Privacy Settings
Granular per-user controls (stored in `privacy_settings` table):
- **Last Seen:** Who can see when you were last online
- **Online Status:** Who can see "Online" indicator
- **Profile Photo:** Who can see your picture
- **About:** Who can see your about text
- **Read Receipts:** Toggle blue ticks globally
- **Group Privacy:** Who can add you to groups
- **Call Privacy:** Who can call you

If privacy settings hide something → backend API automatically redacts the field.

### 11.17 📤 Export Chat
1. User opens ExportChatModal → selects date range
2. Frontend filters messages from local state
3. Generates downloadable `.txt` or `.html` file
4. Browser `download` attribute triggers file save

### 11.18 🔍 Universal Search
1. User opens UniversalSearchModal → types search term
2. Frontend searches across ALL chat message objects in local state
3. Returns matching messages with contact name + timestamp context

### 11.19 🚨 Panic Wipe
Emergency privacy feature:
1. `DELETE /api/messages/panic-wipe`
2. Backend finds ALL messages where user is sender OR receiver
3. For each message → broadcasts WebSocket deletion event to all involved parties
4. All messages purged from DB
5. Both parties' UIs clear those messages instantly

### 11.20 📷 Media Sharing
1. User selects file → `POST /api/media/upload` (multipart)
2. File saved in backend `/uploads/` folder
3. Message sent with `isMedia: true, mediaUrl, mediaType, fileName, fileSize`
4. Receiver sees inline image/video preview or download button for docs

### 11.21 📍 Location Messages
Messages have `latitude` and `longitude` fields — can send location pin in chat.

### 11.22 🤖 AI Assistant (16 Features)
All accessible from ChatWindow AI panel → any feature → AI processes → returns response + privacy report.

