## 12. Request Flow Diagrams

### 12.1 Login Flow
```
Click Login → AuthContext.login(username, pwd)
    → apiFetch("/api/auth/login", POST, {username, pwd})
    → AuthController.login()
    → AuthService.authenticate()
    → UserRepository.findByUsername()
    → BCrypt.matches(input, stored hash) ✓
    → JwtUtil.generateToken(username)
    → { token, username }
    → localStorage.setItem("token", token)
    → isAuthenticated = true
    → App re-renders main chat UI
```

### 12.2 Send Message Flow
```
User types → Click Send
    → cryptoEngine.encryptPayload(content) → {ciphertext, iv}
    → stompClient.publish({destination: "/app/chat", body: messageDto})
    → [WebSocket] Backend MessageController.processMessage(@Payload)
    → MessageService.saveMessage() → PostgreSQL INSERT
    → messagingTemplate.convertAndSend("/topic/messages/receiver", response)
    → messagingTemplate.convertAndSend("/topic/messages/sender", response)
    → Both ChatContexts: subscription receives message
    → cryptoEngine.decryptPayload(content, iv) → plaintext
    → setMessages(updated) → localStorage.setItem(CHAT_STORAGE_PREFIX, ...)
    → ChatWindow re-renders with new message bubble
```

### 12.3 AI Feature Flow (Summarize Example)
```
Click "Summarize Chat"
    → Build transcript from current chat messages
    → [If cloud AI selected] → show privacy permission modal
    → User allows → apiFetch("/api/ai/summarize", POST, {text: transcript})
    → apiFetch adds Authorization: Bearer {token}
    → AiController.postSummarize(AiRequestDto)
    → AiService.getChatSummary(transcript)
    → executeWithReport(promptManager.getSummarizePrompt(transcript))
    → AiProviderManager.selectProvider() → Gemini (if API key set)
    → GeminiAiProvider.generate(promptText)
    → RestTemplate.postForObject("https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/...", body)
    → Parse response → extract text
    → Return AiReportResponse { responseText, provider: "Gemini", processingMode: "Cloud", 
                                sentOutsideDevice: true, processingTimeSeconds: 2.3, status: "Completed" }
    → Frontend displays summary + privacy transparency card
```

### 12.4 Incoming Call Flow
```
Caller clicks "Call" button
    → CallContext.startCall(contactUsername, "audio")
    → navigator.getUserMedia({audio: true}) → localStream
    → stompClient.publish("/app/call/signal", {type: "call-request", callerUsername, callType: "audio"})
    → Backend: /topic/calls/{receiverUsername} → receiver's CallContext triggered
    → Receiver sees IncomingCallOverlay (Accept / Reject)
    → Receiver clicks Accept → Creates peer connection → createAnswer()
    → PUBLISH /app/call/signal {type: "answer", sdp}
    → ICE candidate exchange via /app/call/signal {type: "candidate"}
    → WebRTC P2P connection ✓ → Audio streams flowing directly
    → Either user clicks End → {type: "call-end"} broadcast
    → POST /api/calls → CallRecord saved
    → /topic/callhistory/ broadcast → both see updated call history
```

